---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../../data/site';
import { personId, personSchema, websiteId, websiteSchema } from '../../lib/identity';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const root = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://sangtruong.me');
const canonical = new URL(withBase('/work/curren'), root).href;
const publicRepo = 'https://github.com/sangtrx/curren';
const jsonLd = [
  personSchema(root),
  websiteSchema(root),
  {
    '@type': 'CreativeWork',
    '@id': `${canonical}#case-study`,
    url: canonical,
    name: 'Curren — Quantitative Research & Trading Systems',
    description: 'Public, intentionally bounded case study of Curren, an independent quantitative research and trading-systems project by Sang Truong.',
    author: { '@id': personId(root) },
    isPartOf: { '@id': websiteId(root) },
    inLanguage: 'en',
    dateModified: '2026-09-10T10:04:00+07:00',
  },
];

const layers = [
  ['01', 'Point-in-time evidence', 'Market evidence is treated as time-bounded source material rather than a mutable spreadsheet of hindsight.'],
  ['02', 'Research & evaluation', 'Hypotheses, features, validation, and selection are kept reproducible and separated from later runtime state.'],
  ['03', 'Guarded runtime', 'Signal lifecycle, risk, execution boundaries, reconciliation, and restart behavior are explicit system responsibilities.'],
  ['04', 'Public verification', 'Only a sanitized, read-only projection crosses into the public product surface. Private research and trading authority stay upstream.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Curren — Quantitative Research & Trading Systems | Sang Truong"
  description="A public, deliberately abstracted case study of Curren: point-in-time quantitative research, reproducible evaluation, guarded runtime state, and a sanitized public verification surface."
  image="og-curren.png"
  imageAlt="Curren quantitative systems case study by Sang Truong"
  pageType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="case container">
    <a class="back-link" href={withBase('/#work')}>← Flagship systems</a>

    <header class="case-hero safe-case-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Independent side project · Solo Builder</p>
      <h1>Research discipline before performance theater.</h1>
      <p class="case-lede">Curren is where I treat quantitative research, live-system state, and public product surfaces as different authorities. The goal is a system that can preserve what was known, what was tested, what is running, and what may safely be shown — without publishing the alpha itself.</p>
      <div class="case-meta">
        <div><span>Started</span><strong>Jun 2026</strong></div>
        <div><span>Role</span><strong>Solo Builder</strong></div>
        <div><span>Claim boundary</span><strong>No guaranteed or validated profitable alpha claimed</strong></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="case-section section-rule safe-split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The engineering problem</p><h2>A backtest, a runtime, and a public dashboard should not share authority by accident.</h2></div>
      <div class="prose-stack">
        <p>Quant systems fail quietly when research can look into the future, when experiment state mutates after selection, when live logic drifts from historical logic, or when a public surface starts exposing private trading state.</p>
        <p>I built Curren around explicit evidence and state boundaries so those failure classes are visible before they become performance claims.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule">
      <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Public system cut</p><h2>Evidence in. Authority stays separated.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-note">This diagram is intentionally capability-level. It omits source identities, feature definitions, research parameters, private repository topology, exchange/account controls, credentials, and production host details.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="safe-architecture">
        {layers.map(([index, title, detail]) => (
          <article>
            <span>{index}</span>
            <div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{detail}</p></div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule safe-split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">What this demonstrates</p><h2>Systems thinking across research and runtime.</h2></div>
      <div class="decision-list">
        <article><strong>Causality.</strong><p>Point-in-time evidence and versioned computation keep hindsight from quietly entering research inputs.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Evaluation discipline.</strong><p>Selection and validation are treated as governed processes rather than a single attractive backtest.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Research/runtime parity.</strong><p>Historical, replay, and streaming paths are designed around shared semantics instead of independent copies of strategy logic.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Operational state.</strong><p>Lifecycle, risk, reconciliation, failure, and restart behavior are first-class concerns around any execution path.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule public-surface">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What is public</p>
        <h2>A deliberately boring read-only edge.</h2>
        <p>The public `sangtrx/curren` repository exposes a sanitized developer surface: read-only API/client/CLI/MCP contracts and verification-oriented projections. It is intentionally not the strategy generator or private trading control plane.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button ghost" href={publicRepo}>View public repository ↗</a>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule privacy-panel">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Deliberately withheld</p><h2>The alpha is not the portfolio artifact.</h2></div>
      <p>Private source identities, feature definitions, signal parameters, model internals, execution credentials, account state, trading databases, operational controls, hostnames, machine names, and unreleased performance evidence are excluded. A technical interviewer should be able to judge the engineering without receiving a blueprint for the strategy.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule principle-panel">
      <blockquote>Statistical evidence, execution readiness, and live profitability are different claims.</blockquote>
      <p class="muted">Curren is designed to keep them different. The public case study proves the discipline and system boundaries, not an investment return.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="case-section section-rule case-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore more</p>
      <h2>See the broader AI systems work.</h2>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href={withBase('/resume')}>Full résumé</a><a class="button ghost" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>Contact</a></div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .safe-case-hero h1 { max-width: 12ch; }
  .safe-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .85fr 1.15fr; gap: clamp(40px, 8vw, 100px); align-items: start; }
  .prose-stack p { margin-top: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .safe-architecture { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .safe-architecture article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 72px 1fr; gap: 24px; padding: 28px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .safe-architecture article > span { color: var(--accent); font: 650 .78rem/1 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .safe-architecture h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  .safe-architecture p { margin: 0; max-width: 68ch; color: var(--muted); }
  .public-surface { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 40px; }
  .public-surface > div { max-width: 760px; }
  .public-surface p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--muted); }
  .privacy-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: clamp(36px, 8vw, 110px); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 94%, var(--accent)); padding-inline: clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .privacy-panel p:last-child { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.02rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .safe-split, .privacy-panel { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .public-surface { align-items: start; flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
